  "notes": "Tasklet built + maintains the live RSG deck directly via Slides API (do NOT ask Grok to rebuild). Scope = RSG's three portfolio destinations: The Red Sea + AMAALA + Thuwal. Jeddah dropped 2026-07-01 per Jaideep (no real N30-range sea link to The Red Sea/AMAALA); NEOM Sindalah + Eastern Province/Bahrain dropped earlier. Structure inherits the 24-slide Minor gold hospitality standard, trimmed to 17 (3 destinations + 3 marquee unit-econ appendix). Economics reworked per Jaideep: 15 paid transfers/day, fares reduced (~$85-95/seat), $1M CAPEX/vessel, real boat-only marquee BPs (Shura->Ummahat St Regis/Nujuma; AMAALA Yacht Club->Triple Bay Four Seasons/Six Senses; KAUST Harbour->Thuwal Private Retreat). No SOM/SAM/TAM/GMV ladder (hospitality standard). Images: N30 KSA composites, market-specific backgrounds, navy cinematic scrim, hosted from public repo raw URLs (plates pinned to 06cfe0c2, logo 45e63f28). Thuwal plate = private coral-islet N30 composite. Grok promotes amaala-triple-bay-ksa + thuwal-private-retreat-ksa to destination nodes and mints within/between corridors (spec: handoff/GROK-SPEC-red-sea-global-thuwal-2026-07-01.md).",
